### Block 2 — Declared limitations

| Limitation | Impact |
|---|---|
| No access to ShinKu's current source code | The `ShinKuSource` interface may or may not match existing abstractions. The isolated ClassLoader implementation requires a security audit. `TitleMatcher` needs calibration against real library title data; the 85% similarity threshold is a starting point that may need adjustment. |
| No specified minimum Android version | `WorkManager` and `ForegroundService` require notification-permission handling on Android 13+. The isolated ClassLoader works from API 14, but APK signature verification requires specific APIs. Periodic dead-source detection via `WorkManager` needs to account for battery restrictions on Android 12+. |
| Unknown current implementation state | ShinKu may already have a partial source system or downloader, or a dead-source detection/migration mechanism, which would change the scope of these steps. |
| Unspecified development resources | The extension system is the highest-complexity feature in this block. A smaller team may need to subdivide it into: (a) interface + internal sources, (b) ClassLoader + external sources. Bulk migration's testing complexity (many source/title combinations) calls for a dedicated unit-test suite for the matcher. |

