📋 PROPOSAL: INTEGRATE KOTATSU-MULTI-PARSERS AS A DYNAMIC PLUGIN SOURCE

🎯 THE PROBLEM: PARSER FRAGMENTATION

Kototoro already includes built-in native parsers and integrates the full Kotatsu-Redo parser library. However, the Kotatsu parser ecosystem is fragmented across multiple repositories:

Repository Maintainer Status
kotatsu-parsers-redo Kotatsu-Redo Active
kotatsu-parsers YakaTeam Active
kotatsu-parsers TamerAli-0 Active
kaisoku-parsers glitch-228 Active
kotatsu-parsers hany18h Active
kototoro-parsers skepsun Active

Each repository contains unique parsers for different manga sources. Currently, Kototoro users can only access the parsers bundled with the app (native + Kotatsu-Redo). To access parsers from other repositories, users would need to:

1. Clone each repository
2. Build the JAR files manually
3. Convert them to Dalvik bytecode using the d8 dexer
4. Import them via the "Import Plugin (.jar)" button

This is impractical for most users.

---

💡 THE SOLUTION: ONE-TAP PLUGIN INSTALLATION

Shebyyy's kotatsu-multi-parsers repository already solves the build and distribution problem. It automatically compiles parsers, converts them to Android-compatible Dalvik bytecode, and publishes them as .jar releases using GitHub Actions.

JAR File Source Repository
Kotatsu-Redo.jar Kotatsu-Redo/kotatsu-parsers-redo
YakaTeam.jar YakaTeam/kotatsu-parsers
TamerAli-0.jar TamerAli-0/kotatsu-parsers
glitch-228.jar glitch-228/kaisoku-parsers
hany18h.jar hany18h/kotatsu-parsers
skepsun.jar skepsun/kototoro-parsers

The proposal is simple: Add https://github.com/Shebyyy/kotatsu-multi-parsers as a built-in plugin repository in Kototoro's "Installed Plugins" section, following the same pattern already established for Mihon and Aniyomi extension repositories.

